# Append to /etc/fstab: the writable footage partition (3rd partition on the
# card; OS partition goes read-only via `raspi-config` > Performance > Overlay FS).
# cli/dashberry-install appends this automatically (by PARTUUID) when it builds
# the card — this snippet stays as the manual-install reference.
# data=ordered + commit=1: the 1 s journal commit forces each ~1 s MP4
# fragment's data blocks to the card, so a hard power cut (every ignition-off,
# and an impact that kills 12 V) loses ~1-2 s, not the ~5+ s that the default
# commit interval leaves in the page cache.
/dev/mmcblk0p3  /data  ext4  defaults,noatime,data=ordered,commit=1,nofail  0 2
